name:           lithon-examples
version:        0.1.0.0
synopsis:       Lithon demos — the hello-triangle gates
description:    End-to-end demos driving the generated @lithon@ binding. The primary
                executable renders a triangle offscreen on any Vulkan 1.3 device
                (lavapipe included), writes a PNG, and probe-asserts pixels — the
                phase-3 design gate. @triangle-sdl@ presents the same triangle in an
                SDL2 window through @VK_KHR_swapchain@. @sdl3-raw@ draws a triangle
                raw through @sdl3-bindgen-sys@ — that package's usability gate — and
                @shmup@ is the apecs Shmup example, playable, running on and rendering
                through the same bindings. Not published.
homepage:       https://github.com/jtnuttall/lithon#readme
bug-reports:    https://github.com/jtnuttall/lithon/issues
author:         Jeremy Nuttall
maintainer:     jeremy@jeremy-nuttall.com
license:        BSD-3-Clause
license-file:   LICENSE
build-type:     Simple

